{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 31, :comments ["And its taste was like wafers made with honey — and further on it says: והיה טעמו כטעם לשד השמן. Our Rabbis explained: like honey for infants, oil for the elderly. But I say according to its plain sense: when they eat it as is, without grinding, it is like a wafer in honey. Just as nuts before grinding and pounding are sweet, but further on it is written: וטחנו ברחים או דכו במדוכה — therefore והיה טעמו (like oil) oily, like nuts that become oil after pounding, and likewise olives; and therefore it is written here וטעמו — there [another manuscript reading has] והיה טעמו, for the taste of sweetness changes and becomes the taste of oil." "Like a wafer (צפיחית) — it has no parallel [as a noun elsewhere], but צפחת מים is a vessel." "Gad (גד) — it is a type of legume, round." "Like gad seed, white — like crystal, as it is written further on: ועינו כעין הבדולח. But gad seed is not white."], :book :exodus, :voice :rashbam, :lang :en, :chapter 16, :notes {0 "The parenthetical '(כשמנה)' reflects a variant or marginal gloss in the Hebrew; the passage from 'ולפיכך והיה טעמו' onward appears textually difficult, possibly containing interpolated marginal notes (ס״א = שינוי נוסח אחר), and is rendered hyper-literally without smoothing."}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T14:41:53.238351339Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}